{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And He strengthened… and the children of Israel went out…</b> The meaning is that HaShem needed to strengthen his heart, for he should have paid attention to the manner and order of the departure of the children of Israel, which was with a high hand — and this would declare that the hand of the ruler had been broken from over them. From this he should have been dismayed, except that HaShem strengthened his heart and he entertained the thoughts mentioned above: ״וַיִּרְדּוֹף״ etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:45.072477153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}